// `int`, `string`, and `actor` are declared in every program (their instances can be named; none holds until assigned); an `Act` without `Actor` has the component `actor`.
Act do
  Creates done(actor)
Fact done.
+actor(Alice).
do(Alice).
?done(Alice).
?(int(3) == int(3)).
?!int(3).
?(string(X) == string("X")).
